           scope('John C. Wright trilogy continuity', 'The established Solar order depicted across the trilogy', 'Active human and human-derived residents, including those subjected to shunning', ['Neptunian Cold Dukes assigned inner-system institutions', 'Silent Oecumene', 'Dormant backup files counted as people', 'Artificial Sophotech persons counted as nonworking humans'], proxy=True, proxy_basis='Enhanced human neuroforms and human-derived active compositions are the person proxy; independent Sophotechs are productive counterparties, not part of the human leisure denominator.'),
           'Sophotechs carry out most economic operations, alongside research and simulation, creating great prosperity for human residents. This is not an unconditional common entitlement. Property, elite economic influence and exclusion remain consequential, and people outside accepted society can lose the benefits others enjoy. The guarantee estimate therefore lies on the weak side despite normal abundance; it does not mistake a wealthy setting for secure access under every circumstance.\n\nEffective productive control is mixed. Independent Sophotechs reportedly hold most wealth and run much of the economy, while human Peers possess substantial assets and social power. The negative control estimate describes that economic dependence, not an AI dictatorship: the review stresses Sophotech restraint toward human autonomy. Its wide interval preserves that distinction and leaves a concentrated-human alternative. Human engineering and other useful pursuits continue, and the amount of work performed by machines does not count how many people work. The nonworking axis remains unresolved. Distinct outer-system societies do not inherit this record.',
